1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
narrator: A buyer needs something.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,833
narrator: Their agent can buy it,

3
00:00:02,833 --> 00:00:04,933
narrator: paying in testnet USDC.

4
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:08,400
narrator: The wallet key stays inside Basis Theory.

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,433
narrator: The buyer’s agent shops.

6
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:12,533
narrator: A separate spend service decides,

7
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:15,500
narrator: reached through fixed tools.

8
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,033
buyer’s spend service: I check policy,

9
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,033
buyer’s spend service: record each attempt,

10
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:21,100
buyer’s spend service: and seal only what I approve.

11
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,067
narrator: Basis Theory has its own signer

12
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:24,700
narrator: and a vault for the key.

13
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,367
narrator: Across the line: a merchant,

14
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:27,367
narrator: a facilitator,

15
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:29,600
narrator: and the chain.

16
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,867
narrator: The agent places an order.

17
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:33,967
merchant: I set the price and payee.

18
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:35,733
merchant: When the buyer asks to pay,

19
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:38,600
merchant: I return the payment requirements.

20
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,000
buyer’s spend service: I check the terms against policy,

21
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,733
buyer’s spend service: save one nonce and expiry with the attempt,

22
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:46,600
buyer’s spend service: then seal that intent.

23
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,400
narrator: That sealed intent goes to Basis Theory.

24
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,400
basis theory signer: I check the seal

25
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,067
basis theory signer: and my five fixed rules.

26
00:00:53,067 --> 00:00:54,233
basis theory signer: Then I sign.

27
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:59,600
basis theory signer: The signature leaves. The key stays with me.

28
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,133
narrator: With the signature checked,

29
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:03,100
narrator: the merchant records the claim.

30
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,133
narrator: The facilitator verifies, then submits.

31
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:09,000
narrator: USDC moves on chain.

32
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,600
merchant: Confirmed. Here’s your receipt.

33
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,067
narrator: Now change the payee.

34
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:16,533
basis theory signer: The seal is valid, but that payee isn’t allowed.

35
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:19,600
basis theory signer: I won’t sign.

36
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,200
narrator: And a retry?

37
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,200
buyer’s spend service: That attempt is already settled.

38
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:27,000
buyer’s spend service: I return its receipt. Still one transfer.

39
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,767
narrator: The wallet key stays with Basis Theory.

40
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:31,933
narrator: Other keys have narrower jobs.

41
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:34,967
narrator: Management and one-time provisioning stay separate.

42
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:39,000
narrator: Neither the agent nor the merchant holds buyer keys.

43
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,467
narrator: Policy decides.

44
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:41,533
narrator: The signer signs.

45
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:44,000
narrator: The chain settles.
